{"data": [{"author_id": "44585489", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:14:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117364855879680335"], "id": "2117364855879680335", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z 'Robots cost more to run than to buy' is the line most hardware decks skip. Charging by the hour makes the startup own uptime and maintenance, which is exactly where robotics unit economics are proven or broken.", "url": "https://x.com/SteveXXu/status/2117364855879680335"}, {"author_id": "1494147982517682184", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:29:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117353496597119199"], "id": "2117353496597119199", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Hourly pricing with no upfront cost is the smartest part. A plant manager's real fear isn't the robot failing, it's owning the bill if it does. This answers that on the first call", "url": "https://x.com/LoganWinns/status/2117353496597119199"}, {"author_id": "1322477401", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:12:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117349258537943538"], "id": "2117349258537943538", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z The human-tutor queue seems important. If several robots get stuck at once, does the customer keep working while they wait, or does that become a new bottleneck on the line?", "url": "https://x.com/progerallworld/status/2117349258537943538"}, {"author_id": "704284309", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:59:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117346000729969140"], "id": "2117346000729969140", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z A factory can love your robot and still refuse to buy it.\n\nTutor’s hourly model makes the initial commitment smaller.\n\nMy bet: robotics adoption will accelerate as suppliers get better at absorbing the uncertainty their customers are being asked to carry.", "url": "https://x.com/t_hughesie/status/2117346000729969140"}, {"author_id": "45582017", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:39:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117340932664348699"], "id": "2117340932664348699", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z The human tutor loop could be Tutor’s real moat.", "url": "https://x.com/shuizhuyu/status/2117340932664348699"}, {"author_id": "2008588334537613312", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:26:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117337547575582914"], "id": "2117337547575582914", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z The jobs plants can't fill are real. Robots don't end that hiring problem. They move it.\nNow you need field techs, controls and deployment engineers who keep a fleet up on a live floor, and plant leaders who can run mixed lines.\nThat's its own hard search.", "url": "https://x.com/mikemoriartyATX/status/2117337547575582914"}, {"author_id": "378292434", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:01:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117331205238501705"], "id": "2117331205238501705", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z The part that scales is the human tutor handoff\n\nWhen the robot gets stuck a person teaches it and that becomes training data\n\nHourly pricing with no upfront cost also removes the buying committee fight", "url": "https://x.com/Bijan_Automates/status/2117331205238501705"}, {"author_id": "2041604694569840640", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:59:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117330756712419347"], "id": "2117330756712419347", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 113, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Super insightful, thank you. \"Robotics is this ultimate systems problem\"", "url": "https://x.com/designbyandy/status/2117330756712419347"}, {"author_id": "2020601455527239680", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:57:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117330319439482898"], "id": "2117330319439482898", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Robots that start under human teleoperation have a remote-control channel by design. Who can take over a robot, from where, with what audit trail, matters as much as the model. Identity and signed action logs for every operator and agent belong in v1. #AIsecurity", "url": "https://x.com/lyrie_ai/status/2117330319439482898"}, {"author_id": "2736516054", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:56:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117330133648355485"], "id": "2117330133648355485", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z A robot at $16 an hour with a human tutor on standby means the new job is the tutor. Worth asking where those seats get hired.", "url": "https://x.com/raisetal/status/2117330133648355485"}, {"author_id": "116788949", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:49:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117328307083686301"], "id": "2117328307083686301", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 170, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z a16z's media department head brainstorming B-roll. https://t.co/O5JXORNBjN", "url": "https://x.com/CassidyAWaters/status/2117328307083686301"}, {"author_id": "2101142058237046784", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:39:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117325860403601874"], "id": "2117325860403601874", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z A robot that costs $16 an hour with no upfront cost is cheap enough to compete with warehouse wages once you add benefits. The remote humans who step in when it gets stuck are the jobs to watch, since they train it to replace the next task.", "url": "https://x.com/awi_digest/status/2117325860403601874"}, {"author_id": "2015186975930912768", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:36:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117325042401059303"], "id": "2117325042401059303", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Charging by the hour reframes the whole sale. Nobody buys a robot, they buy completed jobs at a known cost. The winners will be whoever proves uptime and throughput per shift, not whoever builds the flashiest machine.", "url": "https://x.com/vargasjmh/status/2117325042401059303"}, {"author_id": "46498861", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:21:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117321197180555288"], "id": "2117321197180555288", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Three months from a first sales call to a working robot is the detail that matters. Factories do not buy promises, they buy something running on their floor, and the tutor loop means every failure on that floor makes the next shift better.", "url": "https://x.com/raulnogales/status/2117321197180555288"}, {"author_id": "1116857355671691266", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:18:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117320557633184145"], "id": "2117320557633184145", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 36, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117315138105573783", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Somewhere a guy is already blaming the wrong people for this.\n\nhttps://t.co/NFBap1S8c6", "url": "https://x.com/vnmsfx/status/2117320557633184145"}, {"author_id": "1017381153194430464", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:15:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117319625809535293"], "id": "2117319625809535293", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 51, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Human takeover that turns into training data is the right loop. The number I'd want is interventions per robot-hour over time. If it isn't dropping fleet-wide, it's a remote staffing business with very expensive arms.", "url": "https://x.com/ctoincanada/status/2117319625809535293"}, {"author_id": "1213682785262530560", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:04:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117316945997709445"], "id": "2117316945997709445", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 48, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z The most important person in this story is the human tutor. Even robots need someone to teach them. So does your team.", "url": "https://x.com/_DamonScaife/status/2117316945997709445"}, {"author_id": "1560969739488624646", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:59:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117315695935705435"], "id": "2117315695935705435", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 25, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Give me a fuckin job", "url": "https://x.com/cosmiccat2025/status/2117315695935705435"}, {"author_id": "1802300156550721536", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:57:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117315166425448854"], "id": "2117315166425448854", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 45, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Beats shipping those jobs overseas", "url": "https://x.com/iambokensha/status/2117315166425448854"}, {"author_id": "3141637497", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:56:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117315004898677102"], "id": "2117315004898677102", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 98, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Robots by the hour, no upfront cost: that skips the scariest meeting in any factory, the capex one. Curious how fast pilots turn into fleets.", "url": "https://x.com/NilsLiesebach/status/2117315004898677102"}, {"author_id": "458539563", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:49:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117313232557985859"], "id": "2117313232557985859", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 35, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Very unique and novel approach. This will provide relief to companies at a great cost.", "url": "https://x.com/randall_zach/status/2117313232557985859"}, {"author_id": "1776997292601647104", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:41:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117311255736459631"], "id": "2117311255736459631", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Charging by the hour is the real innovation here, not just the robot. Most small warehouses cannot justify a six-figure purchase, but they can test a $16-an-hour robot on one painful shift and measure picks per hour. For cross-border ecommerce, that pricing model could finally", "url": "https://x.com/andyliang17335/status/2117311255736459631"}, {"author_id": "1648787052", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:24:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117306914652737583"], "id": "2117306914652737583", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Everyone assumes a robot startup's moat is the model. Seems to me it's the $16 an hour.", "url": "https://x.com/AnandButani/status/2117306914652737583"}, {"author_id": "1991122899743428608", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:18:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117305476891217930"], "id": "2117305476891217930", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z open source 700tr monthly tokens crushing anthropic(2-3tr) and openai(&lt;2tr); gap increasing fast! thats why $ant decelerating fast! founders cashing out! small models coming on-device, closed labs are fucked. 2tr debt goes up in flames🔥! $TSLA $SPCX $NVDA $AMZN $META #allfucked https://t.co/1WX5VF54uW", "url": "https://x.com/jeowooopn95101/status/2117305476891217930"}, {"author_id": "1589506779783626752", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:11:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117303675941241341"], "id": "2117303675941241341", "in_reply_to_user_id": "64844802", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117297442391744734", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@a16z Robot-as-a-service by the hour kills the CapEx excuse. The labor shortage was a deployment and pricing problem, not a sci-fi one.", "url": "https://x.com/zhuangzhauang/status/2117303675941241341"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "44585489", "name": "Steven Xu | INP Capital", "username": "SteveXXu"}, {"id": "1494147982517682184", "name": "Logan Winn, MBA", "username": "LoganWinns"}, {"id": "1322477401", "name": "Ruslan | Building apps", "username": "progerallworld"}, {"id": "704284309", "name": "Travis Hughes", "username": "t_hughesie"}, {"id": "45582017", "name": "Crio Songo", "username": "shuizhuyu"}, {"id": "2008588334537613312", "name": "Mike Moriarty", "username": "mikemoriartyATX"}, {"id": "378292434", "name": "Bijan | AI for Law Firms | Investor", "username": "Bijan_Automates"}, {"id": "2041604694569840640", "name": "Andy W", "username": "designbyandy"}, {"id": "2020601455527239680", "name": "Lyrie.ai", "username": "lyrie_ai"}, {"id": "2736516054", "name": "Raise | AI, Jobs & Pay", "username": "raisetal"}, {"id": "116788949", "name": "Cassidy Waters", "username": "CassidyAWaters"}, {"id": "2101142058237046784", "name": "AI Wealth Insight", "username": "awi_digest"}, {"id": "2015186975930912768", "name": "Merktop", "username": "vargasjmh"}, {"id": "46498861", "name": "Raúl Nogales 🇪🇸🇺🇸", "username": "raulnogales"}, {"id": "1116857355671691266", "name": "vnmsfx", "username": "vnmsfx"}, {"id": "1017381153194430464", "name": "Lloyd Wilson", "username": "ctoincanada"}, {"id": "1213682785262530560", "name": "Damon Scaife", "username": "_DamonScaife"}, {"id": "1560969739488624646", "name": "Cosmic Cat", "username": "cosmiccat2025"}, {"id": "1802300156550721536", "name": "bokensha", "username": "iambokensha"}, {"id": "3141637497", "name": "Dr. Nils Liesebach", "username": "NilsLiesebach"}, {"id": "458539563", "name": "Zach Randall", "username": "randall_zach"}, {"id": "1776997292601647104", "name": "andy liang", "username": "andyliang17335"}, {"id": "1648787052", "name": "Anand Butani", "username": "AnandButani"}, {"id": "1991122899743428608", "name": "jeowooopn", "username": "jeowooopn95101"}, {"id": "1589506779783626752", "name": "张正恩°", "username": "zhuangzhauang"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2117364855879680335", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlyibfy3a59eof7z2vpso6n9btrx", "oldest_id": "2117303675941241341", "result_count": 25}}